# Concrete public Keccak / SHA3-512 circuit

This ignored component supplies the concrete public hashing primitive needed
by the incomplete B6 IdealFrontierSim machine. It does not implement the whole
public-input framing stage, a proof relation, a native workspace certificate,
or a cryptographic reduction. All full-machine and qualification flags remain
false. No production file, gate, old artifact or Cargo job is changed.

`keccak1600.py` implements the 24 rounds of Keccak-f[1600] as Boolean SSA in
the separately reviewed `bit_ir.py`. Coordinates are `64*(x+5*y)+z`; byte bits
and lane bits are little endian. Theta uses explicit XOR reductions, rho/pi
uses a fixed bijective relabeling, chi uses NOT/AND/XOR, and iota uses fixed
NOTs. Public round constants and rotation offsets are derived from the FIPS
algorithms. No secret lookup, implicit arithmetic, oracle call, or native
instruction is used by this circuit model.

The complete permutation has 115,200 XOR, 38,400 AND and 38,486 NOT nodes,
including 86 set round-constant bits. Compute, copy to an arbitrary disjoint
target and uncompute therefore requires 76,972 X, 539,372 CNOT and 76,800
Toffoli gates. With the existing five-elementary-gates-per-Toffoli convention,
that is **1,000,344 elementary gates and 192,086 clean work bits**. Both
1,600-bit input and output registers are additional. This is the emitted
output-XOR map, not an optimized in-place permutation cost.

`SHA3_512Kernel(n)` handles a fixed public byte length `0 <= n <= 2^20`,
using the source's 72-byte rate, delimited suffix `0x06`, and final `0x80`
padding. It always emits `k = floor(n/72)+1` absorption permutations,
including a fresh padding block after an exact rate multiple. Each permutation
is a clean kernel; its work is shared, while all absorption states are retained
until the outer inverse traversal. The 512-bit output is copied and all work
returns to zero. An empty message has one untouched dummy input bit because
the generic IR requires a nonempty input; either bit value has the same digest.

The resulting complete fixed-length sponge counts are:

```
X        = 2*k*76,972 + 6
CNOT     = 2*k*539,372 + 32*n + 518
Toffoli  = 2*k*76,800
work     = 192,086 + 1,600 + 8*n + 3 + 1,600*k bits
oracle calls = 0
```

The factor of two on each clean permutation accounts for the outer sponge's
reverse traversal. Caller input and output registers are additional. Length
is static circuit shape; choosing an adversarial length, checking public-input
shape, encoding variable data, allocating maximum registers and coherently
selecting among lengths are not provided by this component. No full P0/P1
count can omit those obligations.

The selected Rust correspondence is `iroha_zkp_vole::hash::Sha3_512` and its
`xor_into`, `read_from`, update and finalization methods, plus the public
framing/profile consumers. These hashes are observations, not a compiler
semantic proof or a complete dependency closure. The backend H_mu/H0/H1/etc.
remain restrictions of the named ideal base function in the proposed hybrid;
this concrete SHA3 circuit never turns the backend SHAKE implementation into
an ideal independent oracle or grants a new primitive security premise.

The finite tests compare round constants/offsets against independent tables,
rounds and full permutations against a separate word-coordinate model,
SHA3-512 against Python's independent digest at rate boundaries, and emitted
gates against packed independent basis states. The latter checks arbitrary
XOR targets, noncontiguous relocation, all input and guard bits, complete
workspace cleanup and actual emitted gate counts. Basis tests supplement the
explicit reversible construction; they do not exhaust the 1,600-bit domain.

Primary sources:

- [FIPS 202](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.202.pdf),
  sections 3–6 and byte padding in Appendix B. The retained PDF has SHA256
  `1592607831ff0908cc590632ce371c6c95e94025bb1a0c8ae90a4d0ec1ed025e`.
- [Team Keccak specification summary](https://keccak.team/keccak_specs_summary.html),
  fixed coordinate conventions and independent constant/rotation tables.

